So at year $t$, alien $t$ becomes an adult. The pool of donors consists of aliens $j \in \{1, \ldots, t\}$ who are currently adults. Wait, who is an adult?
The problem statement says: "The i-th alien ... will become an adult exactly i years later."
This implies that at year $k$, aliens $1, 2, \ldots, k$ are adults. Aliens $k+1, \ldots, N$ are minors.
When alien $t$ becomes an adult at year $t$, the donors must be the set of *already* adults who have stones.
